     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Anu's school got a new building funded by the state government and a road repaired by the municipality.\n\"Each level has its work,\" said the teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "Union",
     "State",
     "local government"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "India has three levels of government: the Union (central) government, the State governments and local governments such as panchayats and municipalities.\nThe Union government looks after defence, foreign affairs and currency. States look after police, health and agriculture. Local governments look after water, roads and sanitation.\nThe Constitution divides powers so that each level can serve people better."
    }
